15:13:56 [planner] Server: a new module engine/packages/server/src/leaderboards.ts reads existing tables and ranks the boards, so no migration is needed. There is a total level board, one board for each of the sixteen GDD_SKILLS, a net worth board and a guild board. Skill levels come from the skills projection through levelFor and totalLevel in rules. Ties go to whoever reached the XP first, then by name. Net worth is Crowns plus held items, each valued at its Collector price from content, the same price market.ts uses. Escrowed open orders are left out. Guilds are ranked by the summed total level of their members. Every board leaves out Tinkers whose account has a full ban, joining the bans table from 018_admin the same way admin.ts's banOfTinker does. A guild's member count and total also skip those Tinkers. Each board returns the top 50, plus the viewing Tinker's own rank even when they fall below the cut. One route, GET /tinkers/:id/leaderboards/:board, is registered in src/api.ts. It uses the same tinker-ownership auth and error handling as GET /tinkers/:id/guild. Board names are 'total', a skill name, 'worth' or 'guilds'. An unknown board gets the existing 400 reply. There is no story board and no Reckoning board, as the GDD says. Client: fetchers and types go in src/api.ts. A new screen, src/Leaderboards.tsx, follows Guild.tsx: a row of board tabs, a skill picker using SKILL_ORDER and SkillIcon, and a ranked list that highlights the player's own row. A 'leaderboards' Place is added in SideNav.tsx and routed in App.tsx like the other screens. Tests: engine/packages/server/test/leaderboards.test.ts is written like guilds.test.ts. It checks the order on the total, skill, worth and guild boards through the API, checks that a fully banned player is hidden from the boards and from guild totals, checks that an unknown board is refused, and checks that someone else's Tinker id is refused. Open questions: the net worth valuation (Collector price, escrow excluded), the guild ranking measure (summed total level), the top 50 cut, and the tie-break.
